body:
Allright I tested the `StringName` approach, correct me if I misunderstood. [Here](https://github.com/ugursoy/godot/tree/track-cache-stringname) is the branch for it and here is the snippet:

scene/resources/animation.h
```c++
// keeps StringNames until all ids are assigned for all animations
// during ensure_unique_ids() call to prevent deallocation
static inline LocalVector<StringName> track_cache_id_list;
// counter for required ensure_unique_ids() calls before deallocation
static inline int track_update_counter = 0;
bool update_track_cache_ids = false;
```

scene/resources/animation.cpp
```c++
void Animation::_track_update_unique_ids(int p_track) {
       if (update_track_cache_ids) {
               return;
       }
       track_update_counter++;
       update_track_cache_ids = true;
       callable_mp(this, &Animation::ensure_unique_ids).call_deferred();
}

void Animation::ensure_unique_ids() {
       if (!update_track_cache_ids) {
               return;
       }

       for (Track *track : tracks) {
               const NodePath &track_path = track->path;
               const TrackType track_cache_type = get_cache_type(track->type);

               StringName id = StringName(String(track_path) + itos(track_cache_type));
               track->unique_id = (TypeTrackId)id.data_unique_pointer();
               track_cache_id_list.push_back(id); // Keep StringName object alive
       }

       update_track_cache_ids = false;
       track_update_counter--;
       if (track_update_counter == 0) {
               // All IDs are assigned so StringNames can be freed
               track_cache_id_list.clear();
       }
}
``` 

This works too, I did not see any issues in my tests. Just that the `ensure_unique_ids()` overhead is greater (1.75ms compared to 1.24ms in current approach, for 1000 tracks).

Even though this approach is simpler, I would prefer the one in this PR.

> Assuming the ID can be discarded each time, it might be better to iterate through all tracks without retaining previous IDs, checking only if the same cache type exists.

I don't think IDs need to be discarded. It is not necessary and the alternative is inefficient. Only the changed tracks need to have their IDs reassigned to prevent looping through tracks.

> One way to do this, I though it might be a bit of a hack, but you can convert every concatenated path to StringName first, then use only the memory address of the StringName as the int ID. 

I dislike this `StringName` approach. You need to recreate IDs for all tracks from scratch each time. Even node/track rename would trigger the whole loop. (for a smaller cost, because concatanated `StringName` parts are created already). According to my measurements, 1.75ms becomes 1ms on a node rename here, whereas it costs 0.01ms for the current PR version (for 1000 tracks). The overall overhead is greater.

Also, this forces `TypeTrackId` (prior `TypeHash`) to be `uint64_t`, which is slightly slower than `uint32_t` for lookups (in animation mixer).

